course: dictionary
lesson: 3326
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An evening is a time of day. It comes after the afternoon and before night, from about 6 o'clock until bedtime. «In the evening they point east» tells you the time, because the Sun is low and the shadows change direction.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. An evening can also be an event: a «parents' evening» is a time when families visit school to talk with teachers. To find which meaning fits, read the words around it. Is it a time, or is it something that happens at that time?
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies» still makes sense with the time meaning. Check the clues before you decide.
fact: An evening is the time at the end of the day, from about 6 o'clock until bedtime.
fact: «Evening» can also mean an event held at that time, like a parents' evening.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «good evening», «this evening» and «in the evening».
fact: Fireflies are beetles that make cold light in their tails, and «on a summer evening» a field can twinkle with them.
fact: Context clues, such as the words «parents'» or «shadows», help you choose the right meaning.
exercise: «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies.» What does evening mean here? | A time of day, after the afternoon | A school meeting for parents | *A time of day, from about 6 o'clock until bedtime | A morning walk through the field
exercise: Mum says, «We are going to parents' evening on Thursday.» What is a parents' evening? | A morning assembly | A party for grown-ups at night | A test that children take in the dark | *A school event where parents meet teachers
exercise: Which time of day would you say «good evening» at? | Just after you wake up | At midday | At breakfast time | *About 6 o'clock, when the day is ending
test: «In the morning the Sun is in the east, so shadows point west.» According to the text, which way do shadows point in the evening? | *East | South | West | North
test: Which of these is part of an evening at home? | Breakfast cereal | Morning assembly | Midday sun | *Dinner and homework
exam: Ella says a parents' evening is a party at night. Who is right? | Nobody knows what it means | Ella is right, because it happens at midnight | Ella, because it is always a party | *Ella is wrong: it is a school event where parents meet teachers
